  "preamble": "In Albanian, inherited word-initial *s before a vowel appears as gj, the voiced palatal stop [ɟ] (Gheg also [d͡ʒ]): PIE *serpenos > Proto-Albanian *serpena > gjarpër 'snake'. The change ran through voicing to *z and a glide *j before the glide hardened, so it groups with the hardening of inherited *j- (*jama > gjem 'bridle'); in other words *s- gave sh instead (*sākska > shoh 'to see').",
